      "math_academy_id": "q-32010",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$",
      "worked_solution": "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of the identity matrix by $-2$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation  ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}$ to $A.$",
